                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1e1fd921-9eb1-3fa3-a842-a283b888c562",
                        "entry_id": "51ab1991-2086-3158-8693-9627820a1142",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To add a feature or embellishment that makes something uglier; uglify."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ec331c11-00d5-4625-9fd7-6b5e0b7021cf",
                                "sense_id": "1e1fd921-9eb1-3fa3-a842-a283b888c562",
                                "text": "No ugly monument of their ancestors disfigures the church walls, no hideous brick box unadorns the country churchyard, and a plain stone, perhaps moss grown, is all the record of their fathers they can show."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3264e5d3-5be3-477b-837d-967680d03095",
                                "sense_id": "1e1fd921-9eb1-3fa3-a842-a283b888c562",
                                "text": "In connection with this splendid record I want to point a moral (though it will unadorn the tale), for I recently heard a city man say in a public meeting: “Why, these dairymen are getting rich. They have cows that will make a thousand pounds of butter in a year and look what they get for butter.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c04bf473-87f1-4b74-8425-c79bc6bc7fa2",
                                "sense_id": "1e1fd921-9eb1-3fa3-a842-a283b888c562",
                                "text": "Sanchez glosses Garrula quo comix with the familiar warning against female loquacity — \"silence adorns virgins, chattering unadorns them\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bda16ef2-d73a-334b-b422-4089e6ff87dd",
                        "entry_id": "51ab1991-2086-3158-8693-9627820a1142",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To remove the adornments from."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e1b6b06c-5687-4ab5-8e25-56a9786d1a5c",
                                "sense_id": "bda16ef2-d73a-334b-b422-4089e6ff87dd",
                                "text": "Yet, I have long tried to unadorn Myself for you. I would toss all the trinkets And lavalieres into a box to escape Worshiping."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "06b904dd-1064-47a6-b51a-a788beeefe23",
                                "sense_id": "bda16ef2-d73a-334b-b422-4089e6ff87dd",
                                "text": "He alerts them to every conceivable pitfall, unadorns them of every emotional bias, slices through every pie in the sky as if it's lemon meringue."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ebbdf323-3c6a-4696-b672-10a408c5d52c",
                                "sense_id": "bda16ef2-d73a-334b-b422-4089e6ff87dd",
                                "text": "I will unadorn my neck Tugging away the heavy priceless pearls that have hung around my neck and leave my almost invisible neck bare"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
